{
  "_comment": "Union of tool names across every KINETIC_MCP_MODE surface of kineticdata/kinetic-platform-mgnt-mcp-server (https://github.com/kineticdata/kinetic-platform-mgnt-mcp-server), run locally over stdio/HTTP. Two families are unioned here because the tool vocabulary a doc can correctly reference depends on which mode the reader's server is running: (1) the ~280 per-operation `contexts`/`full`-mode names, each REST operation as `core_<operationId>` and/or a `snake_case` alias (most operations appear under both names below) \u2014 extracted from the server.tool(...) registrations at commit de8e428 (src/tools/contexts/*.ts, src/tools/background-jobs.ts, src/server.ts); and (2) the 26 `consolidated`-mode names (the server's DEFAULT mode as of local commit 437e171, not yet pushed/released) \u2014 one tool per resource family, dispatched by `object`/`action` parameters, verified via a live tools/list round trip against the built server. `slim` mode's tools (get_api_spec, execute_api, connect, and a few others) are already covered by the sets above. A name absent from this union is not a real tool in any mode and should be treated as hallucinated. Used by lint-skills.mjs to reject references to tools that do not exist. This server does not (yet) expose a get_context tool in any mode.",
